To create a Java web application for user registration, follow these steps using **Java Servlets**, **JSP**, and **MySQL**. This example uses Maven for dependency management.

### Step 1: Project Setup (Maven)
Create a Maven project and add dependencies in `pom.xml`:
```xml
<dependencies>
    <!-- Servlet API -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>javax.servlet</groupId>
        <artifactId>javax.servlet-api</artifactId>
        <version>4.0.1</version>
        <scope>provided</scope>
    </dependency>

    <!-- MySQL Connector -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>mysql</groupId>
        <artifactId>mysql-connector-java</artifactId>
        <version>8.0.33</version>
    </dependency>

    <!-- jBCrypt for password hashing -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.mindrot</groupId>
        <artifactId>jbcrypt</artifactId>
        <version>0.4</version>
    </dependency>
</dependencies>
```

### Step 2: Database Setup
Create a MySQL database and `users` table:
```sql
CREATE DATABASE webapp;
USE webapp;

CREATE TABLE users (
    id INT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    email VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    password VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
);
```

### Step 3: Registration Form (JSP)
Create `register.jsp` in `src/main/webapp`:
```jsp
<%@ page contentType="text/html;charset=UTF-8" %>
<html>
<head>
    <title>User Registration</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h2>Register</h2>
    <form action="register" method="post">
        Name: <input type="text" name="name" required><br>
        Email: <input type="email" name="email" required><br>
        Password: <input type="password" name="password" required><br>
        <input type="submit" value="Register">
    </form>
    <p style="color: red;">${errorMessage}</p>
    <p style="color: green;">${successMessage}</p>
</body>
</html>
```

### Step 4: User Model Class
Create `User.java` in `src/main/java/com/example/model`:
